From: DKR-R Windows 95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Measure and attribute the time when no guest thread runs

`guest-run` against `wall` leaves a remainder, and on 21 September 2026 that
remainder came out at about a quarter of the frame -- larger than the whole
33.3 ms budget -- by subtracting this instrument's ratio from the renderer's
per-display-list mean. Two instruments with different populations and different
denominators should not be subtracted from one another.

So the remainder is measured here instead: a count of running guest threads and
a stamp at each edge between one and none, which gives the interval exactly
rather than by difference.

It is also attributed. When the last guest thread goes to sleep the renderer is
asked whether it is inside a display list, and the interval is charged to
`rendering` or to `other`. "The guest is waiting for the renderer" and "the
guest is waiting for something else" are different findings and the difference
decides where the next work goes.

`dkr_renderer_busy` is weak for the same reason `dkr_clock_now_us` is:
ultramodern is a dependency and cannot depend back on the game's renderer. A
build without one links and charges every wait to `other`.

Reported beside the existing line, on the same five-second clock:

  [trace][idle] none-running=N us (rendering=N other=N) intervals=N worst=N us share=N%

---
--- a/ultramodern/src/threads.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/threads.cpp
@@ -216,6 +216,39 @@
    would happen with a single global stamp the moment the scheduler switched. */
